Z||000003||Raydar||08-09-2001||07:42 PM||||Wow! That's a new one on me. Is it TPI (like the Fiero) or TBI? The only 3.4 I've ever seen in a truck was called a 3400 (I think) and was in a Pontiac minivan. <BR>Please keep us posted.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000004||loafer87gt||08-09-2001||08:19 PM||||On found this on Olds website. I had no idea either that there was a Vortec 3.4<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR>3400 VORTEC V6 <BR>Smooth, Refined Power and Precise Road Manners Again this year, all Silhouettes are powered by a 3400 Vortec V6 that is one of the most durable and dependable engines offered in any minivan. The 3.4-liter V6 produces 185 horsepower at 5200 rpm and 210 lb.-ft. of torque at 4000 rpm. Improvements to the 3.4L for 2001 include more efficient catalytic converters, a more durable water pump assembly, a longer-lasting drive belt tensioner and improved spark plugs and wires. Also, combined with the more efficient catalysts and a new forward oxygen sensor with a 6.6-watt heating element, an air gap downpipe speeds emissions light-off time by as much as five seconds. The air gap downpipe was used in 2000 for California and Northeast applications and it is now in all Silhouettes, resulting in the minivan’s being certified for national low-emission vehicle (LEV) status, and ULEV status in California and the Northeast. The engine is mated to a four-speed electronic automatic transmission<BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Steve Normington||08-09-2001||08:41 PM||||This sounds like the engine that I have been trying to put into my Fiero for the last 6 months (3.4 L from a 1997 Olds Silhoutte). My advice is don't do it. You will have to get the ECM and wiring from the vehicle it came out of and you will have to fabricate new brackets for the AC, alt, and dogbone. The ECM for this computer also required you to bypass the anti theft system and I don't think that the module by Rodney Dickman will work.||||reg||1
Z||000006||LarryB||08-09-2001||08:51 PM||||If it's the original V6 gas engine from a '95 Chevy or GMC truck it's a 4.3 liter.  That was the only V6 offered in either the S-10/Sonoma, C/K 1500 or 2500, or Blazer/Jimmy that model year.  <P>||||reg||1
